From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:00:00
Subject: [PATCH] guarded the context menu forward against a dead receiver

QWidgetWindow::handleMouseEvent() picks a receiver, delivers the mouse
event to it, and then - for a right button release - synthesizes a
QContextMenuEvent and forwards it to that same receiver. The delivery in
between runs application code, which is free to close whatever was
clicked: the receiver can be destroyed, and with it the widget this
QWidgetWindow belongs to, and therefore this QWidgetWindow. The forward
then reads m_widget and hands a freed pointer to forwardEvent().

Three crashes in one release land on qwidgetwindow.cpp:692 through this
path: a freed receiver reached through QApplication::notify (a vtable
call on the dead widget), the same thing landing in
QGestureManager::filterEvent, and the bare notifyInternal2 frame.

Qt 6 restructured this code and no longer forwards to a receiver that
went away. Guard the receiver and this window with QPointer and skip the
forward the same way; nothing else changes.

diff --git a/src/widgets/kernel/qwidgetwindow.cpp b/src/widgets/kernel/qwidgetwindow.cpp
index f6799af0f4a..eb254333b3b 100644
--- a/src/widgets/kernel/qwidgetwindow.cpp
+++ b/src/widgets/kernel/qwidgetwindow.cpp
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@
 #include <qpa/qplatformwindow.h>
 #include <private/qgesturemanager_p.h>
 #include <private/qhighdpiscaling_p.h>
+#include <QtCore/qpointer.h>
 
 QT_BEGIN_NAMESPACE
 
@@ -673,6 +674,15 @@ void QWidgetWindow::handleMouseEvent(QMouseEvent *event)
     if (!receiver)
         return;
 
+    // Patched: sendMouseEvent() below delivers into application code, which is
+    // free to close whatever was clicked. That can destroy the receiver, and
+    // with it this window's widget and therefore this QWidgetWindow. The
+    // context menu forward then reads m_widget and hands a freed receiver to
+    // forwardEvent(). Guard both and skip the forward instead, which is what
+    // Qt 6 ends up doing.
+    QPointer<QWidgetWindow> self(this);
+    QPointer<QWidget> receiverGuard(receiver);
+
     if ((event->type() != QEvent::MouseButtonPress)
         || !(event->flags().testFlag(Qt::MouseEventCreatedDoubleClick))) {
 
@@ -686,7 +696,8 @@ void QWidgetWindow::handleMouseEvent(QMouseEvent *event)
         event->setAccepted(translated.isAccepted());
     }
 #ifndef QT_NO_CONTEXTMENU
-    if (event->type() == contextMenuTrigger && event->button() == Qt::RightButton
+    if (!self.isNull() && !receiverGuard.isNull()
+        && event->type() == contextMenuTrigger && event->button() == Qt::RightButton
         && m_widget->rect().contains(event->pos())) {
         QContextMenuEvent e(QContextMenuEvent::Mouse, mapped, event->globalPos(), event->modifiers());
         QGuiApplication::forwardEvent(receiver, &e, event);
